<http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/assertion> {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/maynardsmith-hitchhiking> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/maynardsmith-hitchhiking> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Genetic hitchhiking (selective sweep)" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/maynardsmith-hitchhiking> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "When a favourable mutation sweeps to fixation, it reduces genetic variation at closely linked neutral sites, and the reduction is larger the tighter the linkage relative to the strength of selection." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/maynardsmith-hitchhiking> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/TestableHypothesis> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/maynardsmith-hitchhiking> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "the relative heterozygosity H_{after}/H_{before} at a neutral site at recombination fraction c is an increasing function of c/s that tends to 0 as c/s \\to 0; the affected region has a width of order s in recombination units, up to logarithmic factors in N" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/maynardsmith-hitchhiking> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Assumptions: a single sweep from a new mutation, deterministic allele-frequency trajectory, two loci. Formal status: proved under these approximations (later refined in coalescent treatments). Background selection produces a similar correlation between diversity and recombination." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/maynardsmith-hitchhiking> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/proposedTest> "Test for a positive correlation between neutral diversity and local recombination rate across the genome, and for diversity troughs around sites of recent adaptive substitution, while modelling background selection as the alternative." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/maynardsmith-hitchhiking> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hypothesisType> "model-theorem" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/maynardsmith-hitchhiking> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "John Maynard Smith (1974) The hitch-hiking effect of a favourable gene" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/maynardsmith-hitchhiking> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://doi.org/10.1038/356519a0> .
}
